(4039166, 571858, 64918, '<td valign="top">Apart from being an absolutely superb shot technically it fits the challenge imaginatively (and even humurously) - not just ''qualifying'' on account that there''s a wing in the picture somewhere the bird is looking at its wing and inspecting it. The wing IS the subject. A deserved first place indeed, and one amongst a very high standard of entries too.</td>', 'Apart from being an absolutely superb shot technically it fits the challenge imaginatively (and even humurously) - not just ''qualifying'' on account that there''s a wing in the picture somewhere the bird is looking at its wing and inspecting it. The wing IS the subject. A deserved first place indeed, and one amongst a very high standard of entries too.', '2007-08-29 16:32:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4039187, 573315, 50695, '<td valign="top"><b>critique club</b> <br/> <br/>focus is good, colors are good. <br/> <br/>the composition is one of a photographer trying to get the subject into frame. in other words, not particularly inspired, but serviceable. The bird is in an interesting position. I get a sense of struggle. beyond that, it is what it is: a bird taking off from a pier. to improve, I would suggest seeking out more complex stories or mysteries. don''t answer all the questions the photograph asks.</td>', 'critique club  focus is good, colors are good.  the composition is one of a photographer trying to get the subject into frame. in other words, not particularly inspired, but serviceable. The bird is in an interesting position. I get a sense of struggle. beyond that, it is what it is: a bird taking off from a pier. to improve, I would suggest seeking out more complex stories or mysteries. don''t answer all the questions the photograph asks.', '2007-08-29 16:35:39.000000', NULL, 0),
